# Implementation Plan - Robust Storage Provisioning & Accurate Metrics

This plan fixes the issue where storage provisioning fails due to inaccurate space reporting and lack of node fallback.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This change modifies both the Python Host Service and the NestJS Backend. Ensure the Python `app.py` is redeployed or restarted on the storage nodes after applying changes.

## Proposed Changes

### Host Service (Python)

#### [MODIFY] [app.py](file:///c:/Users/Punith/LaaS/host-services/storage-provision/app.py)
- Update `get_host_space()` to use `zfs list -p -H -o available,size datapool/users`.
- This ensures the "Available GB" reported to the backend accounts for ZFS reservations and quotas, not just raw pool capacity.

### Backend (NestJS)

#### [MODIFY] [node.service.ts](file:///c:/Users/Punith/LaaS/backend-new/src/node/node.service.ts)
- Modify `selectStorageNode()` to:
    - Collect *all* candidate nodes that meet the space + headroom requirements.
    - Sort them by available space (Descending) so the "Best Fit" node is tried first.
    - Change return type to `Promise<Node[]>` or provide a new method `getStorageCandidates()`.

#### [MODIFY] [storage.service.ts](file:///c:/Users/Punith/LaaS/backend-new/src/storage/storage.service.ts)
- Update `provisionUserQuota()` to:
    - Request candidate nodes from `NodeService`.
    - Iterate through the candidates in a loop.
    - Attempt provisioning on the current node.
    - If the node returns a 507 (Insufficient Space) or 503, log a warning and try the next node.
    - Only throw a final error if all candidates fail.

